course: dictionary
lesson: 15451
title: Sterling: money, silver and praise
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them tell you which one you need. «Prices in the shop are in pounds sterling.» Here sterling is money, because pounds comes right before it. Ask: is the word a thing, a description, or a value?
explain: «The ring was sterling silver, with a tiny stamp that read 925.» Here sterling describes what the ring is made of. Try your meaning in the sentence: "The ring was excellent silver" does not fit the stamp, so the clue points to a kind of silver that is very pure.
explain: When sterling means excellent and reliable, it describes work or effort. «Her sterling effort helped the team win.» Try your meaning in the sentence: "Her excellent and reliable effort helped the team win" still makes sense, so you have it right.
fact: Pound sterling is the money of the United Kingdom, and its main unit is the pound (£).
fact: £1 = 100 pence.
fact: Sterling silver is silver that is 92.5% pure, and it is often stamped 925.
fact: «You've done sterling work» means very good, reliable work.
fact: Sterling can be a noun for money or silver, and an adjective when it means excellent.
exercise: «Prices in the shop are in pounds sterling.» What does sterling tell you about the prices? | A kind of silver | A type of weather | Very old | *The money used in the UK
exercise: «The necklace was sterling silver, with a tiny stamp that read 925.» What does sterling tell you? | It is the name of the shop | The necklace is very old | The necklace is made of gold | *The silver is 92.5% pure
exercise: «Coach Patel said, "You've done sterling work today!"» What does sterling mean here? | Cheap and quick | Silent and still | *Excellent and reliable | Very cold
test: «£1 is worth 100 pence.» How many pence make one pound sterling? | *100 | 10 | 1000 | 50
test: «Her sterling effort helped the team win the match.» Which word means about the same as sterling here? | *Excellent | Wet | Late | Weak
exam: «The stall sold sterling silver rings.» What does sterling mean here? | A pound note | Very old | Stormy weather | *Silver that is 92.5% pure
